---
description: Diary entry rules for Forward to Fjord check-ins
alwaysApply: true
---

# Diary entries — exact words only

When the user provides narrative text for a check-in diary entry, reproduce it verbatim. No paraphrasing, no summarising, no added context, no prefixes, no embellishment.

If the user provides no narrative text, write only the bare factual route note in this format:
> From → To (~X km). [One factual sentence if something notable happened, e.g. road name or condition.]

Never add opinions, colour, or invented detail to diary entries.

If the user corrects a diary entry, replace it exactly as instructed and commit without asking for confirmation.
